NAME
       tuned-adm - choose the tuning profile of the tuned service

SYNOPSIS
       tuned-adm list
       tuned-adm active
       tuned-adm recommend
       tuned-adm profile PROFILE...
       tuned-adm off
       tuned-adm verify

DESCRIPTION
       The tuned service adjusts many kernel and device settings at once to
       suit how the machine is used: saving power, handling heavy network
       traffic, running as a virtual machine, and so on. A set of such
       settings is a profile. tuned-adm lists the profiles, shows which one
       is in use and switches to another.

       tuned must be running (systemctl enable --now tuned). The chosen
       profile is remembered and applied again at every boot.

       Some profiles shipped with RHEL 9:

       balanced
              A middle way between speed and saving power.

       powersave
              Save as much power as possible.

       throughput-performance
              Settings for high throughput on a physical server.

       latency-performance, network-latency
              Quick responses, at the cost of power.

       network-throughput
              Fast network transfers.

       virtual-guest
              For a machine running inside a virtual machine.

       virtual-host
              For a machine that runs virtual machines.

       desktop
              Based on balanced, for interactive use.

COMMANDS
       list   List the available profiles with a description, and the active
              one.

       active Print the profile in use now.

       recommend
              Print the profile tuned suggests for this machine (for a virtual
              machine: virtual-guest).

       profile PROFILE...
              Switch to PROFILE. Several names merge their settings.

       off    Stop tuning (no profile).

       verify Check that the profile's settings are all still in effect.

EXAMPLES
       See which profile is active and which one is recommended:

           tuned-adm active
           tuned-adm recommend

       Switch to the recommended profile:

           tuned-adm profile virtual-guest
           tuned-adm active

       Use a profile for heavy network traffic:

           tuned-adm profile network-throughput

FILES
       /usr/lib/tuned/
              The profiles that come with tuned.

       /etc/tuned/
              Your own profiles, and active_profile (the chosen one).

SEE ALSO
       tuned(8), sysctl(8), systemctl(1)
